[Test]
public void TestLastIndexOf()
{
    // Given an ArrayList
    ArrayList arrList = new ArrayList();

    // And an element x
    int x = 42;

    // When we calculate the LastIndexOf of x
    int New_Ret = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

    // Then if the return value is -1, old list size is not -1
    Assert.IsTrue(New_Ret == -1 || arrList.Count != -1);
}
```
This test is checking if the `LastIndexOf` method returns -1, but the size of the list is not -1. This seems to be a contradiction, since the size of an empty list should be 0, not -1.
